### Manual checks for the two APIs. Works with the VS Code REST Client or JetBrains HTTP Client.

@catalog = http://127.0.0.1:5056
@flights = http://127.0.0.1:5057

### Catalog: list conferences
GET {{catalog}}/conferences

### Catalog: one conference (case-insensitive)
GET {{catalog}}/conferences/WORLD-AI-SUMMIT-AMSTERDAM-2027

### Catalog: book (201), then send again with the same key (200, same booking)
POST {{catalog}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"conferenceId": "world-ai-summit-amsterdam-2027", "travellerName": "Les Jackson", "idempotencyKey": "demo-1"}

### Catalog: bookings, newest first
GET {{catalog}}/bookings

### Catalog: cancel (replace the reference)
POST {{catalog}}/bookings/CONF-XXXXXXXX/cancel

### Flights: search by city or airport code
GET {{flights}}/flights?origin=LCY&destination=Amsterdam

### Flights: book
POST {{flights}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"flightId": "lon-ams-british-airways-ba724", "travellerName": "Les Jackson", "idempotencyKey": "demo-1"}

### Flights: bookings
GET {{flights}}/bookings

### Fault: next 3 GETs on the catalog return 503 (then self-heal)
POST {{catalog}}/admin/fault
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": 503, "count": 3, "method": "GET"}

### Fault: flight bookings return 400 until cleared
POST {{flights}}/admin/fault
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": 400, "method": "POST", "pathPrefix": "/bookings"}

### Fault: inspect
GET {{flights}}/admin/fault

### Fault: clear
DELETE {{flights}}/admin/fault
